        "id": 191586,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-20T15:25:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It could be that there isn't too much to say about Bunker specifically. He doesn't seem to be invloved in any major side storys or events that don't already involve the Freedom Five, nor does he seem to go through any major character changes or crucibles. He has only&nbsp;one dedicated nemesis in FrightTrain who will maybe be covered later with the&nbsp;Vengful Five and doesn't have his own book post the&nbsp;\"War Stories\" era.&nbsp;He kinda is who he is and always was and is that throughout the SotM storyline. There isn't even a story to tell about someone else taking the Bunker suit or the technology. So I'm not sure what else there was to say that episode.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>See, I thought the same for a good long while, until info starting coming out about Fort Adamant and the Sentinels, particularly given the research into the OblivAeon Shards and the TermiNation event. &nbsp;I feel like these barely got touched on during the episode, which is odd, considering Bunker's role within those.</p>",
